# Onikiri Mk.I — microSD partition layout (MBR/DOS)
#
# Partition map (all sizes in 512-byte sectors):
#
#  p1  FAT32   boot     sectors   2048–133119   (  64 MiB)  U-Boot, kernel, DTB, boot.scr
#  p2  squashfs system  sectors 133120–1181695   ( 512 MiB)  read-only system root
#  p3  ext4    userdata sectors 1181696–…        (rest of card)  persistent user data
#
# IMPORTANT — image reflash behaviour
# ------------------------------------
# The flashable .img.xz is sized to cover ONLY p1 + p2 (577 MiB).
# The partition table at sector 0 still defines p3 at sector 1181696.
# Because Etcher writes only the bytes contained in the image file,
# everything at or after sector 1181696 on the target card is left
# completely untouched.  User data in /userdata therefore survives
# a reflash of the system image.
#
# On a blank card the first-boot script (S05userdata-init) creates an
# ext4 filesystem on p3 and populates the required directory tree.
# On a reflashed card it detects the existing filesystem and skips init.
#
# Minimum card size: 8 GiB.
# The p3 size below targets a nominal 8 GiB card; the first-boot script
# runs `growpart` + `resize2fs` to fill larger cards automatically.
#
# Reference sector arithmetic (512-byte sectors):
#   BOOT_START  =    2048
#   BOOT_SIZE   =  131072   (  64 MiB)
#   SYS_START   =  133120
#   SYS_SIZE    = 1048576   ( 512 MiB)
#   USERDATA_START = 1181696
#   USERDATA_SIZE  = 15595520  (~7.43 GiB, fills remainder of 8 GiB card)

label: dos

1 : start=2048,    size=131072,   type=c, bootable
2 : start=133120,  size=1048576,  type=83
3 : start=1181696, size=15595520, type=83
